Subject: [PATCH] tas2555: decode fault register and return status read errors

R104 contains sticky DAC/amplifier faults; R108 contains DSP interrupt
outputs. Do not overwrite R104 before decoding its bits. In particular,
R108 bit 3 is reserved and is not a brownout indicator.

Read DSP flags first so a failed R108 read cannot discard a clear-on-read
R104 fault. Preserve accumulated software errors on failed reads. Return errors through the ALSA
TAS_Status getter rather than reporting an apparently successful query.
Keep existing fault-response actions and protection settings unchanged.

Reference: TI SLASE69B, B0_P0_R104 and B0_P0_R108 register tables.
Upstream-Status: Pending
Assisted-by: Briar

diff --git a/tas2555-codec.c b/tas2555-codec.c
--- a/tas2555-codec.c
+++ b/tas2555-codec.c
@@ -446,7 +446,7 @@ static int tas2555_errcode_get(struct snd_kcontrol *pKcontrol,
 		pValue->value.integer.value[0] = errCode;
 
 	dev_dbg(pTAS2555->dev, "tas2555_errcode_get = 0x%x\n", errCode);
-	return 0;
+	return nResult;
 }
 
 static int tas2555_errcode_put(struct snd_kcontrol *pKcontrol,
diff --git a/tas2555-core.c b/tas2555-core.c
--- a/tas2555-core.c
+++ b/tas2555-core.c
@@ -391,11 +391,17 @@ int tas2555_get_errcode(struct tas2555_priv *pTAS2555, unsigned int *pErrCode)
 {
 	unsigned int errcode = 0;
 	unsigned int nValue = 0;
+	unsigned int nDspFlags = 0;
 	int nResult = 0;
 
+	/* A failed DSP read must not discard a clear-on-read R104 fault. */
+	nResult = pTAS2555->read(pTAS2555, TAS2555_FLAGS_2, &nDspFlags);
+	if (nResult < 0)
+		return nResult;
 	nResult = pTAS2555->read(pTAS2555, TAS2555_FLAGS_1, &nValue);
+	if (nResult < 0)
+		return nResult;
 	if (nResult >= 0) {
-		nResult = pTAS2555->read(pTAS2555, TAS2555_FLAGS_2, &nValue);
 
 		if (nValue & 0x04) {
 			errcode |= TAS2555_ERROR_CLKPRESENT;
